    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, all tests pass). \n\nDone. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Change**: Added a derived-on-read `locality` field to the owner response, following the same pattern as the existing computed fields (`membershipTier`, `displayName`, etc.) rather than persisting it \u2014 since it's a pure function of the already-stored `city`.\n\n**Files touched**:\n1. `mapper/Localities.java` (new) \u2014 the fixed city-to-region table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) with `forCity(city)` returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n2. `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` expression that delegates to `Localities.forCity(owner.getCity())`.\n3. `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (which generates the `OwnerDto` field).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass (`NSW` for a Sydney owner, `UNKNOWN` for a random city) and the full build is green.",
